From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <spolack+claude@mailbox.org>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 23:20:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] udht: never block on the relay sockets

Both ends of the relay between unet-dht and unetd were blocking UNIX datagram
sockets: the client socket unet-dht sends on, and the socketpair end it hands
to unetd over SCM_RIGHTS, which unetd keeps as pex_unix_tx_fd. unetd's
pex_fd_cb() already treats EAGAIN as "drop this one", but never saw it, and a
blocking sendmsg() on a full queue stalls the sender. With the DHT node
running inside unetd's own process that stall would be a deadlock, since the
same thread is the one that would drain the queue.

Open the client socket non-blocking, set O_NONBLOCK on the end passed to
unetd, and let dht_sendto() lose a packet quietly when the queue is full
instead of treating it as a lost connection.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019FGFD5nZ9AL3AdMi7SfYSg
---
 udht.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/udht.c b/udht.c
index a369005..cdb8a37 100644
--- a/udht.c
+++ b/udht.c
@@ -94,6 +94,8 @@ int dht_sendto(int sockfd, const void *buf, int len, int flags,
 
 	ret = sendmsg(sockfd, &msg, flags);
 	if (ret < 0) {
+		if (errno == EAGAIN || errno == ENOBUFS)
+			return ret;	/* queue full: this packet is lost, nothing else */
 		perror("send");
 		if (errno == ECONNRESET || errno == EDESTADDRREQ ||
 		    errno == ENOTCONN || errno == ECONNREFUSED)
@@ -316,7 +318,13 @@ udht_open_socket(const char *unix_path)
 	int sfd[2];
 	int fd;
 
-	fd = usock(USOCK_UNIX | USOCK_UDP, unix_path, NULL);
+	/*
+	 * Neither end of the relay may block: unetd's pex_fd_cb() handles
+	 * EAGAIN on its end, and a full queue must drop a DHT packet rather
+	 * than stall whoever sends it. With unetd and the DHT node in one
+	 * process a blocking send on a full queue would never be drained.
+	 */
+	fd = usock(USOCK_UNIX | USOCK_UDP | USOCK_NONBLOCK, unix_path, NULL);
 	if (fd < 0)
 		return -1;
 
@@ -324,6 +332,7 @@ udht_open_socket(const char *unix_path)
 		close(fd);
 		return -1;
 	}
+	fcntl(sfd[0], F_SETFL, fcntl(sfd[0], F_GETFL) | O_NONBLOCK);
 
 	dht_unix_fd = fd;
 	dht_fd.fd = sfd[1];
